# 2. UNEXPAND COMMAND

## What is `unexpand`?

`unexpand` does almost the opposite of `expand`.

It converts sequences of spaces into TAB characters.

### Basic Syntax

```bash
unexpand filename
```

---

## Example

```bash
printf 'Name    Age    City\nJohn    25     Bangalore\n' > data.txt
```

Run:

```bash
unexpand data.txt
```

---

## Convert only leading spaces

A useful option is:

```bash
unexpand -a data.txt
```

The `-a` option converts spaces throughout the line where possible.

---

## Real-world example

Suppose you have a text file with many spaces and want to reduce its size or make it tab-separated.

You can use:

```bash
unexpand -a data.txt
```

This can be useful when preparing structured text files.

---

## Practice Exercise

Create:

```bash
printf 'Name    Age    City\nAlice   21     Delhi\nBob     24     Mumbai\n' > students.txt
```

Try:

```bash
